Queue Workers (Background Job Processing)
=========================================

For optimal performance with multiple users and large datasets (1 crore+ records),
run these THREE workers in separate terminals:

Terminal 1 (CSV Import Worker - Highest Priority):
npm run queue:work
- Handles: CSV imports, Database-to-Database transfers
- Concurrency: 3 (can process 3 CSV imports simultaneously)
- Priority: 5 (highest)

Terminal 2 (Audience Queue Worker - Medium Priority):
npm run queue:audience
- Handles: Bulk audience assignments, Subscriber imports
- Concurrency: 1 (one heavy job at a time to prevent memory issues)
- Priority: 3 (medium)

Terminal 3 (Maintenance Queue Worker - Lowest Priority):
npm run queue:maintenance
- Handles: Duplicate removal, Heavy cleanup operations
- Concurrency: 1 (one very heavy job at a time)
- Priority: 1 (lowest - runs when system is less busy)

Note: These workers can handle 15+ concurrent users uploading 1 crore+ records each.
Jobs are queued and processed based on priority, ensuring system stability.


